MCP - Model Context Protocol 

MCP acts as the standardized communication layer between an AI application/LLM and external capabilities such as tools and resources.
It allows AI applications or LLMs to access external tools, resources and prompts.
It contains three main components which is Host, Client and server.
Server hanldes the data acess and tools by connecting database, api's or tool.
Clients act as communication bridge between a host and server that converts a requests into structured format.
Host coordinatee communication between multiple clients and servers, and handle orchestration logic for end to end task processing.
MCP uses JSON-RPC 2.0 messages for communication between an MCP client and an MCP server.


Rosources: geeksforgeeks, databricks and MCP

