The follow-up tool executed successfully.
The agent completed the task in 2 iterations.
The LLM generated analysis and recommendations for both customers.


4. Important issue we found:

LLMs can sometimes invent information that is not present in the MCP data.
Strong prompts and verified data can reduce this problem, but we need to keep testing it.
This showed why grounding and validation are important when building AI agents.

The agent works, but the LLM can mix verified customer facts with general industry information.
We need to keep customer-specific analysis based only on information available through MCP.
Facts, general observations, and recommendations should be clearly separated.


